    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d897">

                <pb facs="0814" n="807" xml:id="pg807"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.01 Provisional/5: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Counselor of Embassy in China</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Lockhart</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary
                        of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Peiping</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1937-12-14T16:00:00+08:00">December 14, 1937—4
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received December 14—8:40 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>822. Embassy’s 820, December 14, 11 a.m.<anchor n="26" xml:id="d897-f1"/> The new
                    government is named the “Provisional Government of the Republic of China”. It
                    consists of one Executive Committee under Wang Keh Ming, a Legislative Committee
                    under Tang Erh Ho, and a Judicial Committee under Tung Kang. Under the Executive
                    Committee there are four “Ministries”: Public Safety under Chi Hsieh Yuan,
                    Education and Culture under Tang Erh Ho, Justice under Chu Shen, and
                    Reconstruction and Rehabilitation under Wang Yi Tang. Kao Ling Wei becomes Mayor
                    of Tientsin and Governor of Hopei Province. Chiang Chao Tsung continues as Mayor
                    of Peiping. All but Chiang are old Anfu clique men.<anchor n="27"
                        xml:id="d897-f2"/> Evidently it is the intention of the Provisional
                    Government to create some sort of permanent government for “all China”, after
                    which they will resign. Its members state that the Provisional Government has
                    the <hi rendition="#italic">de facto</hi> recognition of Japan and hopes to
                    obtain the <hi rendition="#italic">de facto</hi> recognition of other
                    governments.</p>
                <p>Japanese attending the inaugural meeting included Major General Kita, in charge
                    of Japanese special military affairs organ in North China, Colonel Nemoto head
                    of the Peiping special military affairs organ, Major Watanabe of the same
                    office, and Morishima, Counselor of the local government [<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Embassy</hi>].</p>
                <p>Repeated to the Ambassador, Shanghai and Tokyo.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Lockhart</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
